WEBVTT

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.460
Damn! My business equipment just went crazy!

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.420
Damn! Damn!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.810
I might not be able to get there on time!

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.770
Why did I have to work overtime today?!

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.820
Sylia, wait for me for three more minutes.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.990
Well, two more minutes!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.150
Priss and Nene have begun the action already.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.450
What?! Why didn't they wait for me?!

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.760
What's this? No way!

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.970
Why me?!

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.520
Not again! This always happens
at the worst time!

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:50.960
Good job.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.170
Why, thank you!

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.720
Yahoo! Thanks, thanks!

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.600
I'm finally here.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.060
See, Priss? I can do a good job,
just like this time!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.900
How long do you intend to
stand there? I'm going.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.490
Wait for me!

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.800
I guess it's because I used too much power.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.770
This part, it's manufactured by Genom, isn't it?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.150
A part is a part, no matter who manufactures it.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.990
You don't like parts made by Genom, do you?

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.740
Well, not a great deal I guess.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.910
These are certainly more precise
than other makers'.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.740
Mackie, give me a torque wrench.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.790
Sure!

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.330
Here.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.050
Cheese...

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.640
Nene's gotten stronger, hasn't she?

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.940
I guess.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.400
Sure she has.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.980
Before I joined the team,

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.190
it was just the two of you doing
this for the longest time, right?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.820
I feel like I'm being left behind
by both of you again.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.700
You have your regular job.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.660
Wow...

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.700
What?

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.660
You care about me like that!

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.880
I have to leave Tokyo for a little bit.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.880
Where are you going?

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.210
My parents' house.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.880
I have to go back there for a short while.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.470
It's a lot of trouble for me, but...

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.640
Can you tell Sylia about it?

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.850
Sure, why not?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:01.940
I simply love to watch boomers at work!

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.360
Regarding the Showhamm Project,

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.950
the Umbrella will be completed on schedule.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.370
However...

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.160
A problem on this side?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.120
It's the Dragon that stores the
energy sent from Umbrella.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.960
Construction of the underground
stream is behind schedule, so...

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.480
Disorder of the stratum caused by
the earthquake wasn't allowed for?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.020
It was greater than we expected.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.230
Also, the consumption of boomers
for underground work was quick.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:48.440
What do you think the completion
of this project means?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:54.370
It's a drastic solution to Earth's
energy and resource shortage.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.790
Genom will take control of the
economy as an energy industry.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:07.300
Do you know why I live like this
without any organ transplants?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:13.430
I am able to keep myself alive
by using these machines.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.760
These machines live on energy.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:22.940
I bought all the boomers and
facilities created by Dr. Stingray,

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:27.770
because I thought the boomer
was a new form of humanity.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:35.280
I was wrong. They are friends of
mankind. I can't be one of them.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:39.490
The Showhamm Umbrella that the
boomers are constructing

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.710
will create unlimited power, and
because of that power,

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:47.210
I'll be able to become one with the
system which controls this planet.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.960
I don't think there's any meaning
to just extending one's life.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.390
Mason, I'm going to become the
system of this planet Earth.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.680
By becoming the system,

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.770
I will guide humanity and
boomers in the true path.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.270
Forever!

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.490
Momma!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.660
Momma!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.290
It's all an old man's nonsense after all.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.930
The Boomer Crushers haven't made it there yet?

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.810
What a cruel thing to call them!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.480
If the Knight Sabers heard that, they'd cry.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:50.650
I've heard that the Chairman
has lost his interest.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.400
Why don't you leave the matter to the AD Police?

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.070
I'm not asking your opinion.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:08:00.700
What are you going to do while
Dragon construction is halted?

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.880
The Metro Express is so fast! I'm here already!

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.130
I have lots of time.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.470
I don't want to waste any of it.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.780
Underground...

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.610
I understand. It's an underground
stream that stores the energy

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.700
sent from that stupid umbrella.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.120
What a fantasy for such a pitiful old man!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.500
They're doing something while
Dragon construction is stopped,

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.960
but they're not using an
internal department.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.630
They're using outside specialists
to do something.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.210
Brian Mason!

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:03.560
Dr. Stingray is in the middle of an experiment.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.310
You're a good girl, aren't you?

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:12.400
A good girl doesn't bother her dad
while he's working. Right?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.820
Good girl!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.500
That man must have a target. But what?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.330
I'm home!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.690
I'm home!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:37.120
Linna's back!

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.580
What? Why didn't you call from the station?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.540
Sorry, I'm late.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.210
What are you doing standing there?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.000
Make proper greetings to the guests!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.800
I'm home, everybody.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.800
Linna, I've heard you're a
career woman in Tokyo!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.220
Do you have a boyfriend there?

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.390
I don't think this girl is that attractive!

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.480
I'm not good at dealing with my relatives.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.750
Oh, sorry. I didn't help you finish cleaning up.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.920
It's okay, since you've just got home.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.590
My home's comfortable since I'm used to it.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.630
Honestly speaking, I've just
started living by myself in Tokyo,

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.430
and it's too early to come back,
so I didn't like this idea, but...

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.100
Are you eating properly? Are you
getting used to work there?

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.600
I'm fine!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.520
Your father is so happy that you're back.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.440
What? He didn't look like it!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.150
He's not the kind of person to show emotion.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.360
He sure isn't.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.370
Delicious...

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.120
How long can you stay here?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.500
I'm going back to Tokyo tomorrow,
because I'm a new employee.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.870
I can't take long vacations.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:10.210
Can you stay at least until
the day after tomorrow?

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.630
I have to take you somewhere tomorrow.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:15.170
Just as I thought.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:18.630
I wondered why you insisted that I
come back for the memorial.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.760
This is from one of your father's
business customers, so...

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.930
An arranged date.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.220
Have you found anything interesting in Tokyo?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:31.480
You used to tell us that you'd find
something that you'd love to do.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.770
For the first time your Dad had to
give up what he wanted to do.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:35.820
I found it.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.860
I think I've found it.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.070
Well, I think I've been setting
goals like that all along.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.660
That's not such a bad thing.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.040
Really?

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.510
That move... That powered
suit is no ordinary one.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.230
I wonder if this suit is an
inheritance from Dr. Stingray.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.110
Show me the staff list of the Wiz Lab.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.940
Who is not confirmed dead among these?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.870
Nigel Kirkland...

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.160
An engineer in the boomer facility, wasn't he?

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:33.170
Do you know what your prototype looked like?

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.880
No, I do not know.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:40.510
Stingray didn't intend to create an
android capable of independence.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:52.940
Meth. It means death in Hebrew.

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.980
Just one letter Stingray erased
from a word on your forehead.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.950
Emeth. It means truth.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:07.490
The owner of this funny Tower
of Babel lost this letter.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.870
He thinks you're his friends.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.790
He believes that only faithful
golems will worship him.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.050
I will make the essential boomer awaken.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.100
That's the reason I was born a human being.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.350
You understand me, don't you?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.350
No, I don't.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.810
I know you don't understand.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.400
You're still just a golem.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.860
I thought Rosenkrantz was most
capable of helping realize my goal

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:43.610
and at the same time, the biggest obstacle.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.660
I guess he isn't.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.840
You hate wearing a kimono that much?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.590
My hairstyle isn't right for one.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.600
It not a big deal, right? It's just
a simple greeting today.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:14.140
Excuse me, but I came here
today for you, Mom,

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.230
but I don't think this is fair.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:22.030
I've just started living in Tokyo,
and I haven't done anything yet.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:24.070
I even went to junior college in this town for you.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:27.490
I think it wouldn't hurt you if you
let me enjoy a little more freedom.

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:29.120
We didn't mean it like that.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.160
We simply agreed that there's a
nice young man in town, so...

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.120
I don't...

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.170
Your companion has arrived.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:40.630
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:41.630
Oh, no...

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.410
Your name is Mr. Masaki, right?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.370
Yes.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.330
This isn't cool at all, is it?

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.540
That's why I don't like my hick
country hometown.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:20.000
I can't believe that this arranged
date system is still alive here.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.590
I told my parents that I didn't like this idea.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.300
See! It's such a pain, isn't it?

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.510
It's not that bad an idea for me.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.680
Ms. Linna, you're working in Tokyo, aren't you?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.640
Well, yes.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:40.140
That's great! I went to college in Tokyo.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.690
I see...

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.900
It was right after the earthquake,
and the place was full of boomers.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.150
That place was so bustling.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.740
I didn't have any qualms about
helping my father in his business,

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.740
so I returned right after graduation.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.870
You went to Tokyo after you
stood up for yourself,

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.080
because you had something you
wanted to do, didn't you?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.920
They didn't need to tell you
about things like that.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:05.250
That's wonderful.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.090
I desperately wanted to go to Tokyo,

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:14.720
even though I hadn't decided
what I wanted to do.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:18.020
I'd thought I could find what
I wanted to do quickly.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.180
Actually, I did find what I want to do.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:25.690
But even if I get uptight, my
existence means nothing.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.150
Nothing I do changes anything.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.990
I'm envious of you, Mr. Masaki.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:34.870
Because you understand what you
can do and where you need to be.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:39.330
I wonder if the place you should
be is waiting for you.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:47.300
Sorry, I'm getting too personal, aren't I?

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.260
I guess, since we've just met.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:55.800
I want to know you better, to
start becoming friends.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.820
All right, the shift is over!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.320
Good morning!

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.240
Well, see you later!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.290
Hey, get out of my way!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.290
Sorry, but can you stay overtime
for a little while?

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:30.000
Remember that incident in an
outlying area the other day?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.630
So what?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:35.340
There's an anonymous report from
a so-called citizen of good will.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.600
I said, "So what?!"

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:40.720
Knight Sabers attacking a boomer.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:44.560
The scene was recorded with a
camcorder. Please analyze it.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.360
Why do you need to bring stuff like this to me?

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:50.610
What do you mean?

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:54.610
Nothing! I'll accept this request
just for you, Leon-pyon!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.990
Wait a second! What the hell is "Leon-pyon"?

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.780
Why me?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:03.500
Hey, I'm asking you a question,
what's this "pyon" thing?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.500
What the hell is a so-called citizen of good will?

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.080
Are you listening to me?!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.380
Cut it out!

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.750
Your attitude is not suitable for
a person asking for a favor.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:14.300
But she called me "pyon", and
the last time she was...

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.380
Forget about it and let's go.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.130
Wait a second, Daley!

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.270
Oh geez, we were recorded so perfectly.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:32.400
Cool! I'm so cool, aren't I?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.650
Wait a second...

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.910
Why were they taking pictures
before we got there?

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.950
Someone was waiting for us?

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:44.580
Emergency dispatch request from the G4 area.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.960
All nearby PC and BV, please
respond immediately.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.810
I can't leave the office now.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:08.890
What's the target?

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.190
A trial model for a military attack boomer!

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.770
It's huge and very strong, I've heard.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.780
We need to get paid more than
the regular rate then.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:22.950
Is that so, in Tokyo?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.330
Yes, it is!

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:27.000
I'm might want to go back there
after hearing a story like that.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.250
Really?

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.130
Ah, excuse me!

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:37.800
Linna, where are you now?

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:40.510
Priss hasn't told you?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.720
Can you take action?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.890
I can't leave the office now, and
Priss is about to get there,

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.850
but I'm sure it'll be impossible for
her to deal with the boomer alone!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.810
I can't go, because now I'm with...

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:59.530
Next Episode

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:05.160
A huge mad boomer has appeared in the city.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:09.210
Buildings are destroyed, and
even missiles are flying.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.000
It's definitely a military boomer.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.330
Size is not this boomer's only strong point.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.290
Neither Nene nor Linna are
able to make it here now,

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.510
so I guess I'll have to deal with it by myself.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:20.680
It might be not so bad that I
have no rival in this race.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.720
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
